From a9b40b0547062494bd54a186f9d5dce30274658f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:02:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] clocksource/samsung_pwm: tick broadcast for S5P6818 SMP

No delivered arch-timer PPIs on S5P6818, so the single global PWM channel is the
only clockevent. On ARCH_NEXELL rate it below the per-CPU dummy_timer so it is
installed as the tick BROADCAST device - otherwise secondaries never tick and
RCU stalls. Verified: 8 CPUs, stable under load.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/clocksource/samsung_pwm_timer.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/samsung_pwm_timer.c b/drivers/clocksource/samsung_pwm_timer.c
index 0ab28f9c6..bd448fb2d 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/samsung_pwm_timer.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/samsung_pwm_timer.c
@@ -275,6 +275,20 @@ static void __init samsung_clockevent_init(void)
 	pwm.clock_count_per_tick = clock_rate / HZ;
 
 	time_event_device.cpumask = cpumask_of(0);
+#if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_ARCH_NEXELL)
+	/*
+	 * S5P6818 (octa A53): the ARM generic-timer PPIs are not delivered to
+	 * the non-secure kernel, so this single global PWM channel is the only
+	 * real clockevent. For SMP it must serve as the tick BROADCAST device
+	 * for the per-CPU dummy_timer clockevents (CONFIG_DUMMY_TIMER, rating
+	 * 100) on all cores - otherwise the secondaries never get a tick and RCU
+	 * stalls. Rate it below the dummy timer so it is NOT claimed as CPU0's
+	 * per-CPU device and is installed as the broadcast device instead (the
+	 * vendor BSP does the same with rating 50). It keeps ONESHOT, required
+	 * for oneshot broadcast.
+	 */
+	time_event_device.rating = 50;
+#endif
 	clockevents_config_and_register(&time_event_device,
 					clock_rate, 1, pwm.tcnt_max);
 
